      "Proper duct design isn't just about connecting Point A to Point B. Key factors include: static pressure calculations to ensure adequate airflow, velocity management to control noise levels, balancing dampers for even distribution, proper sizing (oversized ducts waste money, undersized ducts starve spaces), and transition design to minimize turbulence and pressure drop.",
